Design a parity checker that computes the odd parity bit for an 8-bit input. The module counts the number of high bits in the input data and assigns the output parity_bit to 1 if the count is odd, indicating that there is an odd number of 1s in the input. If the count is even, the parity_bit will be set to 0.
module top_module(
  input [7:0] data_in,
  output reg parity_bit
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [7:0] data_in,
  output reg parity_bit
);reg [2:0] count;
  integer i;

  always @(*) begin
    count = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
      count = count + data_in[i];
    end
    parity_bit = (count % 2 == 1);
  end

endmodule

