description:
Design a circuit that counts the number of set bits (1's) in a 32-bit input number. The module takes a 32-bit input and produces a 32-bit output where the value corresponds to the count of bits set to 1 in the input. This functionality is implemented using a combinational logic block that sums the set bits by iterating through each bit of the input.
module top_module(
    input [31:0] input_num,
    output reg [31:0] output_num  // Changed wire to reg
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [31:0] input_num,
    output reg [31:0] output_num  // Changed wire to reg
);reg [31:0] count;
    integer i;

    always @(*) begin
        count = 0;
        for (i = 0; i < 32; i = i + 1) begin
            if (input_num[i] == 1'b1) begin
                count = count + 1;
            end
        end
        output_num = count;  // This assignment is now valid
    end

endmodule

