description:
Design a module that implements HMAC (Hash-based Message Authentication Code) for message integrity and authentication. The module takes a 256-bit message and a 256-bit secret key as inputs and produces a 256-bit HMAC output. It splits the key into two parts, pads the message to align with the block size of the hashing function, and performs XOR operations with the padded key and intermediate hash values. The hashing functionality is simulated through defined functions for padding, XOR, and hashing, ensuring that the HMAC conforms to established standards for secure cryptographic operations.
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] msg,
  input [k-1:0] key,
  output [h-1:0] hmac
);

code:
module top_module(
  input [n-1:0] msg,
  input [k-1:0] key,
  output [h-1:0] hmac
);parameter n = 256; // number of bits in the message
parameter k = 256; // number of bits in the secret key
parameter h = 256; // number of bits in the HMAC value
parameter b = 512; // block size of the hash function

// Split the secret key into two parts
wire [b-1:0] k1 = key[k-1:0];
wire [b-1:0] k2 = key[2*b-1:b];

// Pad the message with zeros to a multiple of the block size
wire [((n+b-1)/b)*b-1:0] padded_msg;
assign padded_msg = {msg, {(b - (n % b)) % b{1'b0}}};

// XOR k1 with the block of zeros that precedes the message
wire [b-1:0] xor_result = k1 ^ {b{1'b0}};
wire [b-1:0] hashed_result = hash(xor_result, k1);

// XOR k2 with the block of zeros that precedes the intermediate hash value
wire [b-1:0] xor_result2 = k2 ^ {b{1'b0}} ^ hashed_result;
assign hmac = hash(xor_result2, k2);

// Define the padding function
function [b-1:0] pad;
  input [b-1:0] data;
  input [b-1:0] key;
  begin
    pad = data ^ key;
  end
endfunction

// Define the hash function
function [b-1:0] hash;
  input [b-1:0] data;
  input [b-1:0] key;
  begin
    hash = pad(data, key);
  end
endfunction

endmodule

