Design a clock phase shifter that alters the phase of an input clock signal based on a specified shift value. The module takes a clock input and an 8-bit shift value, calculating a maximum delay proportional to the input clock frequency and shift value. It generates a shifted clock output by introducing a delay determined by the shift value, effectively allowing for the synchronization or adjustment of clock signals in digital circuits. The output clock phase can be finely controlled, making this design useful in applications like clock recovery or timing adjustments in digital systems.
